gb350: unai can draw a subset of the VRAM rows (two cores sharing drawing)

renderer_set_split(shift, skip): VRAM rows are stripes of 2^shift rows;
stripe s is skipped when bit (s & 31) of skip is set. One core draws with
one pattern, the other (the GB350's second core, corelink service 2) with
its complement, into the same VRAM: every pixel always has the same owner,
whichever buffer the game draws to. skip 0 (the default): every row, no
change.

